OpenClaw v2026.8.1: constrain inferred plugin installation to plugins.allow.

Base: ea806575e6450e4d1efdfc72c19f04be982a1b9b.

Startup convergence treats provider keys inherited from a developer shell as
requests to install official plugins. A VYDRA_API_KEY can therefore trigger an
unrequested installation and capability-consent refusal before Gateway readiness,
even though LobsterAI's restrictive plugins.allow excludes vydra.

Filter the final inferred download candidate set using the normalized allowlist.
Resolve official catalog aliases for comparison without rewriting the actual
installation id. Explicit CLI plugin installation, existing install records,
recorded npm updates, capability consent, and runtime verification are unchanged.
An absent or empty allowlist preserves upstream auto-install behavior.

The included repair tests cover env-only Vydra with excluded/allowed/normalized/
empty/absent allowlists, explicit entries under a restrictive allowlist, both QQ
catalog alias directions, and preservation of skipped existing npm records.

